{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Yitzḥak loved Esav, for game was in his mouth.</b> When his father would ask him, 'What are you doing in the field all day?' he would make excuses and say, 'In order to hunt game to bring food to my father's mouth.' And because he was not to be found with his mother, therefore Rivqah did not love him, and she loved Ya'akov, who was to be found with his mother, and all her longing was upon him. And one may explain that it indicates the time — to tell you that at that time when he would put game in his mouth, at that time alone did he love him; but after he had already eaten from his game, the thing was void and the love was void. But Rivqah loved Ya'akov for nothing, and such love is never void."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:03.864063974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}